\li \subpage page_toolbox_particles_realisation

The particle toolbox provides generated particle models, vertex-associated
storage, sorting, rank-boundary exchange, and temporary interaction sets. It
contains no application physics; extensions add the particle attributes and
update kernels they require.

Particles use the particles-in-dual-tree association: a particle belongs to a
persistent spacetree vertex on the level selected for its interaction radius.
Movement can lift or drop that association across levels. The design is
described in T. Weinzierl et al., [Two particle-in-grid realisations on
spacetrees](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.parco.2015.12.007).

*/
